element that has never been found on earth or anywhere in the universe.
It has been made, the half-lifes of its varioius isotopes has been 
measured and from that we can calculate how much of astatine exist in 
any given time. But still nobody has ever found any astatine and given a 
half-life of the most stable isotope being 8.3 hours that's not surprising.

So astatine, the element number 85, has never been found, but 
statistically there must exist some of it at any given moment.

So is there 92 or 91 natural elements?

